# Build context exclusions for the web image.
#
# `node_modules` is the important one. It is large, it is platform-specific
# (a Windows or macOS tree copied into a Linux build produces confusing native
# module failures), and `npm ci` reinstalls it correctly inside the build
# anyway. Excluding it also keeps the build context from being tens of
# thousands of files, which is the difference between a fast build and a slow
# one.

# --- Dependencies and build output -----------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Secrets and data ------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
../data/
data/

# --- Test and lint artefacts -----------------------------------------------
coverage/
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/

# --- Editors and OS ---------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Scratch ----------------------------------------------------------------
.tmp*
*.log
npm-debug.log*
